  m_Name: 1850 vernacular
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Vernacular Schools (1800s-1930s) '
  info: As immigrant communities grew, vernacular schools were set up to teach in
    Chinese, Malay, and Tamil, ensuring children retained their cultural heritage.
    Chinese-medium schools like Chung Cheng High School were particularly influential.
    However, these schools often lacked funding and standardized curricula, creating
    disparities in education quality.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5115cf0708ef747f380fc999d1132c61, type: 3}
